 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing the town of Cornwall\nto impose a hotel and motel tax; and providing for the repeal of such\nprovisions upon expiration thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S4073",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4073-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §1202-gg-1, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S4073\n\nSPONSOR: SKOUFIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing the town of\nCornwall to impose a hotel and motel tax; and providing for the repeal\nof such provisions upon expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation authorizes the Town of Cornwall in Orange County to\nimpose by local law, a tax on hotel and motel occupancy of up to three\npercent of the charge.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: amends the Tax Law by adding a new section 1202-hh, in\nrelation to the imposition of a hotel and motel tax in the Town of Corn-\nwall.\n\nSection 2: Sets effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation would allow the Town of Cornwall to impose a hotel and\nmotel tax. The rate of such tax shall not exceed 51s of the per diem\nrental rate for each room. Pursuant to the Municipal Home Rule Law, a\ntown may adopt local laws that relate to the levy and administration of\nlocal taxes if authorized by the State legislature.  The Town of Corn-\nwall has requested special legislation which will enable them to collect\na hotel and motel tax in an effort to raise additional revenue for the\ntown.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall expire and be deemed\nrepealed 3 years after such date.\n",
